<title>UK: Imperial Tobacco up on Merrill comment.</title>
<headline>Imperial Tobacco up on Merrill comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Tobacco Plc rose on Friday as analysts at Merrill Lynch repeated an &quot;accumulate&quot; rating on the stock and set a one-year price target of 440p, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 5p at 366 by 0952 GMT.  </p>
<p>Sources said Merrill pointed out the stock had been weighed down by U.S. selling since it was spun off from Hanson but that its above-average yield made it attractive, with earnings growth expected to be at least in line with the market.</p>
<p>Analysts at Merrill were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
